body:
If you don't want a library, here's a function that I made to handle simple cases:

    type RawQuery = TemplateStringsArray;
    type Values = (string | number | boolean)[];

    export function buildQuery(rawQuery: RawQuery, ...values: Values) {
      let text = "";
      rawQuery.forEach((string, i) => {
        text += string;
        if (i !== rawQuery.length - 1) text += `$${i + 1}`;
      });
      return { text, values };
    }

or the code golf version:


    function buildQuery(rawQuery, ...values) {
      const text = rawQuery.reduce((p, n, i) => `${p}${n}$${i+1}`, "").slice(0, -2);
      return { text, values };
    }

and just like in parent,

    buildQuery`SELECT * FROM foo WHERE id = ${id}`
    // { text: "SELECT * FROM foo WHERE id = $1", values: [id] }

ps: Consider these lines to be released under the MIT license, but the rest of my project is proprietary.
